  "notes": "Boot a Doctor Who ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape, wait out the power-up mechanism test, open the service menu, start T.4 SOLENOID TEST and step it with Up through its coils. In repeat mode the ROM pulses the selected output and prints its own name and wire colours for it, so each step pairs a printed name with the public address PinMAME published. An output checkpoint makes a missed menu edge fail the run: T.4 must pulse solenoid 1 after it starts. The selected name blinks, so three frames 0.35 s apart are taken at every step.",
  "version": 1,
  "watch_switches": [
    22
  ]
}
